## 🎯 The Core Framework: 5 Phases

The framework follows a structured approach that **prevents rework** and **ensures stakeholder alignment**:

```
DISCOVER (Week 1)
├─ Don't write code yet
├─ Understand the business question
├─ Draft project charter
└─ Validate data availability

DEFINE (Week 1-2)
├─ Lock down metrics definitions
├─ Mock up final deliverable
├─ Create data validation plan
└─ Get stakeholder sign-off

DEVELOP (Week 2-4)
├─ Build iteratively
├─ Show work-in-progress weekly
├─ Incorporate feedback early
└─ Maintain documentation

DELIVER (Week 4-5)
├─ Tailor to your audience
├─ Lead with the answer (BLUF)
├─ Make insights actionable
└─ Professional polish

DOCUMENT (Week 5)
├─ Write lessons learned
├─ Document code and logic
├─ Create runbook if recurring
└─ Knowledge transfer to team
```

---

## 💡 Key Principles

### **1. Define "Done" Before You Start**
Never begin coding until you know what the final deliverable looks like. Mock it up first.

### **2. Show Work-in-Progress Early**
Don't wait until Week 4 to show your work. Weekly check-ins starting Week 1 prevent surprises.

### **3. Spend Time on Requirements to Save Time on Rework**
10 hours spent on requirements saves 40 hours of rework. Front-load your discovery.

### **4. The Best Analysis Gets Used, Not the One That's Perfect**
Deliver 80% of the value quickly, then iterate based on feedback. Don't chase perfection.

### **5. Data Validation Before Analysis**
Trust but verify. Validate your data sources early before building complex logic.

